{{# Latin only, deliberately, and it is now a single file.

    Which CJK subsets a page needs depends entirely on its content, and the
    blog's top page is a variable list of posts, so preloading kanji buckets
    is guesswork that goes stale as soon as the posts change. The Latin slice
    is the exception: the site chrome is Latin, and Japanese posts are full of
    Latin — product names, "AI", "IT", numerals — so it is needed on every
    page. The CJK subsets are left to ordinary CSS-driven discovery. #}}
<link
  rel="preload"
  href="/fonts-ja/textface-100-normal-100-700-latin.woff2"
  as="font"
  type="font/woff2"
  crossorigin="anonymous"
>
<!-- ===== font-preload-ja.vto TEMPLATE END ===== -->
